Follow-up query, minutes after the SUCCEEDED result above, no intervening
commands sent:
  gz ground truth master position: 0.79999999999979787   (fully closed)
  diag_box pose: x=0.29526434404038321 y=0.23057882126315032 z=0.019999594960673803
                 (gz model -m diag_box -p: RPY -1.570800 -0.000003 -1.405370
                 -- tipped on its side)
  -> box ejected from its 0.49214/0.13332/1.11692 spawn point to the floor,
     ~1.1m net displacement, after the action had already reported a
     successful stall.

Root-cause reading (mechanism checked against controller source, not
guessed -- see docs/HANDOFF_M3.md "06 retried..." section for citations):
GripperActionController::check_for_success's stalled branch marks the ROS
action SUCCEEDED but never calls set_hold_position() or otherwise changes
command_struct_.position_ away from the original goal (0.8). The position
command interface keeps being written 0.8 every control cycle regardless of
action status, so sustained force continues toward full closure after
"success" until it eventually ejects the object.

